      <li><code>href="file.dita"</code> links to the topic. <code>href="file.dita#topic/element"</code> links to an element inside it that has an <code>@id</code>; the topic id is required in the fragment because one file can hold several topics.</li>
      <li><code>@scope="external"</code> says the target is outside the project and is not to be resolved or copied. <code>@format="html"</code> says what kind of thing it is, so the processor does not try to parse it as DITA.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;link&gt;</code> is the same reference as <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> but as a list entry in <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code>. It takes <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> for the text when the target has no title, and <code>&lt;desc&gt;</code> for a short description. The HTML5 output shows the description as a tooltip (the <code>title</code> attribute of the link), not as text under the link.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-related-links-on-the-remaining-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Related links on the remaining topics<a href="#step-2-related-links-on-the-remaining-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/recording-your-first-track.dita</code> A cross-reference in the context, a new <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code> with two links, and a <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> block after <code>&lt;/taskbody&gt;</code>.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n+++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@\n   <taskbody>\n     <context>\n       <p>This task walks you through making your first audio recording.\n-      You need a microphone connected to your computer.</p>\n+      You need a microphone connected to your computer.\n+      If you are new to audio terms such as sample rate and clipping, read <xref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/> first.</p>\n       <note type=\"tip\">For best results, record in a quiet room and position the microphone 15 to 30 cm from your mouth.</note>\n     </context>\n     <steps>\n@@ -46,5 +47,12 @@\n       <p>You now have a recorded audio track in your project.\n       The waveform shows the shape of the recorded audio: louder sounds appear as taller waves.</p>\n     </result>\n+    <postreq>\n+      <p>Trim the false starts (<xref href=\"trimming-audio.dita\"/>), then export the result (<xref href=\"exporting-audio.dita\"/>).</p>\n+    </postreq>\n   </taskbody>\n+  <related-links>\n+    <link href=\"preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n+    <link href=\"removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n+  </related-links>\n </task>"} lang="diff" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/trimming-audio.dita</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n@@ -45,4 +45,8 @@\n       <p>The unwanted audio is gone and the track plays through without a gap.</p>\n     </result>\n   </taskbody>\n+  <related-links>\n+    <link href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n+    <link href=\"exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n+  </related-links>\n </task>"} lang="diff" title="topics/trimming-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/what-is-audacity.dita</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n@@ -22,4 +22,12 @@\n       Whatever the project, Audacity provides the tools at no cost.</p>\n     </section>\n   </conbody>\n+  <related-links>\n+    <link href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n+    <link href=\"installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n+    <link href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n+      <linktext>The Audacity website</linktext>\n+      <desc>Downloads, the manual and the user forum.</desc>\n+    </link>\n+  </related-links>\n </concept>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-audacity.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita</code> This one groups its links. A <code>&lt;linklist&gt;</code> has a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and keeps its links in the order written; a <code>&lt;linkpool&gt;</code> has no title and lets the processor sort and merge its links with the ones the map generates later.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n@@ -6,7 +6,8 @@\n   <shortdesc>Digital audio is sound stored as numbers: samples taken thousands of times a second at a chosen precision.</shortdesc>\n   <conbody>\n     <p>Digital audio is sound that has been converted into a numerical representation.\n-    A few key concepts help you make better recordings and edits.</p>\n+    A few key concepts help you make better recordings and edits.\n+    If you would rather start recording, go straight to <xref href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/> and come back later.</p>\n     <section>\n       <title>Waveforms</title>\n       <p>Sound travels through air as a continuous <term>waveform</term> of pressure changes.\n@@ -72,4 +73,17 @@\n       <lq reftitle=\"The Audacity Manual\">Audio is measured in decibels because the ear hears ratios, not differences.</lq>\n     </section>\n   </conbody>\n+  <related-links>\n+    <linklist>\n+      <title>Put it into practice</title>\n+      <link href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n+      <link href=\"preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n+    </linklist>\n+    <linkpool>\n+      <link href=\"supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n+      <link href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sampling_(signal_processing)\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n+        <linktext>Sampling (signal processing)</linktext>\n+      </link>\n+    </linkpool>\n+  </related-links>\n </concept>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the placement</strong> <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> is a child of the topic, after the body, not inside it. In a task it follows <code>&lt;/taskbody&gt;</code>; in a concept, <code>&lt;/conbody&gt;</code>. The validator rejects it anywhere else.
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-check-your-work" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Check your work<a href="#step-3-check-your-work" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check your work</strong> Format the topics: choose <strong>XML</strong> &gt; <strong>Format</strong> in each changed topic and save it, or choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Project Tools</strong> &gt; <strong>Format Project</strong> to format every file at once. From the command line, run:
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Then choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> in the editor, or run <code>dogsbay-xml check .</code> from the project root. The output looks like this example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full\noutput   clean (full)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and the output of full holds together."} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>This is the first stage with links inside topics. The health check has resolved the <code>@href</code> of each <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> in the map since stage 02; now it also resolves each <code>@href</code> in a topic. Misspell the target of the <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> to <em>Trimming audio</em> in <em>Exporting audio</em> as <code>trimming-audo.dita</code> and check your work. The file still validates, because a broken link is not a grammar error, but the health stage reports it with the file and line, and the check stops. The following output is an example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/topics/exporting-audio.dita:61  @href=\"trimming-audo.dita\" — target not found\n  (run project-health for the full report)\nNot ready: the project itself has faults. The build and the built output were not checked."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Undo the change and check again.</p>
      <p>The health and output stages cover different problems. In <em>Exporting audio</em>, find the <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> to the <em>Choosing a format</em> section. Change the fragment <code>#supported-audio-formats/choosing</code> to <code>#supported-audio-formats/choose</code> and check your work. The source passes the health stage and the DITA-OT build. The link renders and points at an anchor that the page does not have. The output stage reads the built HTML and reports each link that leads nowhere, with the page, the line, and the target. The following output is an example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full\noutput   1 broken link(s)\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full/topics/exporting-audio.html:17  @href=\"supported-audio-formats.html#supported-audio-formats__choose\" — nothing in topics/supported-audio-formats.html has id \"supported-audio-formats__choose\"\nNot ready: 1 link in the built output leads nowhere."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Undo the change and check again.</p>
      <p><code>dogsbay-xml conref-audit</code> checks conref target IDs. It does not check cross-reference links.</p>
      <h2 id="why-links-belong-in-the-map" class="group scroll-mt-20">Why links belong in the map<a href="#why-links-belong-in-the-map" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Every <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> block you wrote here is a statement about how topics relate, stored inside one of the two topics. In stage 09 you organize the map and add a relationship table. Those statements then move to the map, where one <code>&lt;reltable&gt;</code> row says "these topics are related" once and the processor generates the links on both sides. Topics then carry only the <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code>s that the text needs, and the same topic can be related to different neighbors in different guides.</p>
      <p>Writing these links first shows the relationships that the map later generates. Topic-level links are also useful when publishing a topic on its own.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code> before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="the-map-at-this-checkpoint" class="group scroll-mt-20">The map at this checkpoint<a href="#the-map-at-this-checkpoint" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>This lesson adds no topics, so the map does not change. For reference, the complete map at this checkpoint is:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n<map>\n  <title>Audio user guide</title>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n  <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n</map>"} lang="xml" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> in the text; <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> after the body.</li>
      <li>Empty link elements take their text from the target's title.</li>
      <li><code>file#topic/element</code> reaches a section or any element with an <code>@id</code>.</li>
      <li><code>@scope="external"</code> and <code>@format</code> for links out of the project; <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> when there is no title to borrow; <code>&lt;desc&gt;</code> for a blurb.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;linklist&gt;</code> keeps order and has a title; <code>&lt;linkpool&gt;</code> lets the processor sort and merge.</li>
      <li>The check's health stage catches broken references that validation cannot. Its output stage catches links in the built HTML that lead nowhere, such as a wrong fragment.</li>
      </ul>
